  cdType String [not null, default: 'ADD']
  cdApplyOn String
  cdLedgerCode String [not null]
  cdLandingCost Boolean [not null, default: false]
  cdCostAlloc String
  cdBeforeTax Boolean [not null, default: false]
  cdTaxApl Boolean [not null, default: false]
  cdSepPost Boolean [not null, default: false]
  cdUnit String
  cdQtyVal Decimal
  cdWeight Decimal
  cdRate Decimal
  cdAmount Decimal
  cdTaxCode String
  cdHsn String
  cdTaxPerc Decimal
  cdTaxAmt Decimal
  cdSgstPerc Decimal
  cdSgstAmt Decimal
  cdCgstPerc Decimal
  cdCgstAmt Decimal
  cdIgstPerc Decimal
  cdIgstAmt Decimal
  cdCessPerc Decimal
  cdCessAmt Decimal
  cdNetAmt Decimal
  cdRemarks String
  cdIsActive Boolean [not null, default: true]
  cdSrcCdId String
  cdSrcAccYear String
  cdCarryBasis String [note: 'PRORATA | FULL | MANUAL | NONE']
  cdCarriedAmt Decimal [not null, default: 0, note: 'On the SOURCE row: how much has been taken so far. A cache.']
  cdIsDeleted Boolean [not null, default: false]
  cdSyncDate DateTime
  cdCreatedOn DateTime [default: `now()`, not null]
  cdCreatedBy String
  cdModifiedOn DateTime
  cdModifiedBy String
  charge charge_master [not null]
  ledger acc_ledger_master [not null]
  tax tax_rate_master
  company companys [not null]
  branch branch_master [not null]
  sourceCharge txn_charge_detail
  carriedCharges txn_charge_detail [not null]

  indexes {
    (cdId, cdAccYear) [pk]
  }

  Note: 'Per-document applied charges — freight, loading, packing, cash discount, etc.
One row per charge line on a document, shared by every module (sales,
purchase, quotation, GRN, invoice) via the cdDocType discriminator.

Every cd* column except the amounts is a SNAPSHOT taken from ChargeMaster
(and its ledger) at save time, so editing a charge master later never
rewrites what was already invoiced.

public.txn_charge_detail is LIST-partitioned by cd_acc_year, like
sales.sale_bill, sales.sale_order and sales.sale_quotation. Partitions (e.g.
txn_charge_detail_2026_2027) are created by
public.ensure_acc_year_partitions(\'YYYY-YYYY\') — run it whenever a fiscal
year is opened, or every insert fails with "no partition of relation
"txn_charge_detail" found for row". Because Postgres requires every unique
constraint on a partitioned table to contain the partition key, the primary
key is the pair (cdId, cdAccYear): a row is addressed by both, never by the
id alone.'
}

Table txn_transport_detail {
  ttdId String [not null]
  ttdCompanyId String [not null]
  ttdBranchId String [not null]
  ttdTenantId String
  ttdAccYear String [not null]
  ttdDocType String [not null, note: 'SALE_BILL | DELIVERY_CHALLAN | SALE_RETURN | DC_RETURN | STOCK_TRANSFER.
Widened per module as each arrives — PURCHASE_BILL and PURCHASE_RETURN
join when those are built.']
  ttdDocId String [not null, note: 'Polymorphic: NO relation field and no FK, because a child cannot key four
different partitioned parents. The service is what stops a band outliving
its document — the same price TransactionChargeDetail and TxnStatusLog
already pay.']
  ttdDocRefno String [note: 'Snapshot, so a row reads alone.']
  ttdDirection String [not null, note: 'OUTWARD | INWARD — what FROM and TO mean on this row.']
  ttdFromGodownId String [note: 'Set when the FROM side is ours.']
  ttdFromBranchId String
  ttdFromAddrId String [note: 'A listed ship address, when it is one. No FK: the address masters are
company-scoped and a band must survive one being retired.']
  ttdFromName String
  ttdFromAddr String
  ttdFromPlace String
  ttdFromPin String
  ttdFromPhone String
  ttdFromStcd String
  ttdFromGstin String
  ttdToGodownId String [note: 'Set when the TO side is ours.']
  ttdToBranchId String
  ttdToAddrId String
  ttdToName String
  ttdToAddr String
  ttdToPlace String
  ttdToPin String
  ttdToPhone String
  ttdToStcd String
  ttdToGstin String
  ttdTransportMode String [note: 'ROAD | RAIL | AIR | SHIP']
  ttdTransporterId String
  ttdTransporterName String
  ttdTransporterGstin String [note: 'The PORTAL\'s transporterId: a 15-character GSTIN or enrolment id, NOT the
TransporterMaster uuid in ttdTransporterId.']
  ttdLrNo String [note: 'e-way Part-B transDocNo / transDocDate.']
  ttdLrDate DateTime
  ttdDistanceKm Int
  ttdRemarks String
  ttdIsDeleted Boolean [not null, default: false]
  ttdSyncDate DateTime
  ttdCreatedOn DateTime [default: `now()`, not null]
  ttdCreatedBy String [not null]
  ttdModifiedOn DateTime
  ttdModifiedBy String
  transporter transporter_master
  fromGodown godown_locations
  toGodown godown_locations

  indexes {
    (ttdId, ttdAccYear) [pk]
  }

  Note: 'ONE transport band for every document that moves goods.

The band used to be 22 columns repeated on sale_bill, sale_dc, sale_return
and sale_dc_return — 88 definitions of the same 22 facts, which had ALREADY
drifted before anyone noticed: vehicle_id was missing from the DC return and
supervisor_id existed only on the bill. Every future e-way field would have
been four ALTERs, and the fourth is the one that gets forgotten.

NOT for storage. That argument was measured and does not hold: 22 NULL
columns cost about 8 bytes a row, because PostgreSQL keeps NULLs as one bit
each in a row bitmap. One definition instead of four is the whole reason.

Same shape as TransactionChargeDetail and TxnStatusLog — a polymorphic child
keyed by (docType, docId, accYear), LIST-partitioned on the year.

── FROM and TO are POSITIONAL; ttdDirection says what they mean ─────────

OUTWARD (sale bill, delivery challan)
FROM = our godown / branch      TO = the customer\'s address
INWARD  (sale return, DC return)
FROM = the customer\'s address   TO = our godown / branch

The doc register then maps straight across, with no per-document branch:
gdr_dispatch_*  <-  ttd_from_*
gdr_ship_*      <-  ttd_to_*

Whichever side is OURS fills the godown / branch columns; whichever side is
the party\'s fills the address block. Both sides carry both, so a
branch-to-branch move needs no third shape.

The VEHICLE and the CREW are deliberately NOT here — they stay on the
document, because they exist whenever goods move even with no consignment
at all: a POS home delivery has a driver and a van and no transporter, no
LR, no distance, no e-way bill.'
}

Table transporter_master {
  trnId String [pk]
  trnCompanyId String [note: 'NULL = every company.']
  trnCode String
  trnName String [not null]
  trnGstin String [note: 'GSTIN or 15-char enrolment id (TRANSIN) — ck_trn_gstin_len enforces the
length either way.']
  trnIsEnrolmentId Boolean [not null, default: false]
  trnMode String [not null, default: 'ROAD', note: 'ROAD | RAIL | AIR | SHIP']
  trnLedgerId String [note: 'Freight payable ledger, optional. No FK: a transporter may be recorded
long before anybody decides which ledger their freight posts to.']
  trnPhone String
  trnEmail String
  trnAddr String
  trnPlace String
  trnPin String
  trnStateCode String
  trnRemarks String
  trnIsActive Boolean [not null, default: true]
  trnIsDeleted Boolean [not null, default: false]
  trnSyncDate DateTime
  trnCreatedOn DateTime [default: `now()`, not null]
  trnCreatedBy String
  trnModifiedOn DateTime
  trnModifiedBy String
  vehicles vehicle_master [not null]
  transportBands txn_transport_detail [not null]

  Note: 'The transporter on an e-way bill.

sale_bill.sb_vehicle_id has existed in this database with NO referenced
table — and so have sb_driver_id, sb_supervisor_id and sb_loadman_id. This
master and VehicleMaster are what those columns should have pointed at.

trnGstin holds either a GSTIN or a 15-character transporter ENROLMENT id
(TRANSIN), which is why trnIsEnrolmentId exists: the two are the same
length and the portal treats them differently.

NULL trnCompanyId = shared by every company, the house convention for a
master that is not company-specific.'
}

